━━━ stdout
Scaffold a detection rule.

Usage: opentide new rule [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          Object name; the filename is its slug

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Add a configuration block for this platform (repeatable): sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops
          
          [possible values: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops]

      --objective <OBJECTIVE>
          UUID of the objective or signal this rule implements (detection_model)

      --path <PATH>
          File to write, or a folder to write it in (default: the family's objects folder)

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide new rule --name "Suspicious LSASS Access" --platform sentinel --objective <objective-uuid>

━━━ stderr · empty
